1. Function Declaration
A traditional way of defining a function using the function keyword.

j
function login(page) {
  // reusable login function
  return page.goto('/login');
}
Hoisted (can be used before declared)







Function Expression
A function assigned to a variable (can be anonymous or named).


const logout = function(page) {
  return page.click('#logout');
};
⛔ Not Hoisted



Arrow Function (=>)
Introduced in ES6. Shorter syntax, no own this.

const generateRandom = () => Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);




function runTest(callback) {
  console.log("Running test...");
  callback(); // runs whatever you pass
}

runTest(() => {
  console.log("Test logic here");
});





Used when working with await and promises — MUST in Playwright.


async function fillForm(page) {
  await page.fill('#email', 'test@test.com');
  await page.click('text=Submit');
}
✅ Use await inside these.